<slack:paste select="#m1" />

<slack:transform select="#m1,.finding,.said" instruct="Does the message sentence (the fragment whose id starts with #m) make claims that are BACKED or UNSUPPORTED by the other fragments? Name the source ids and quote the shortest backing passage. Meeting turns name their speaker; every fragment is prefixed with its id." from="">
</slack:transform>

<slack:copy id="m2" class="message">Root cause: the checkout service's DB connection pool was sized at 20, and under load we were queueing for connections with a 500 ms timeout — the fix raised the pool to 40 and the timeout to 2s, gated by feature flag `checkout_db_pool_v2`.</slack:copy>

<slack:paste select="#m2" />

<slack:transform select="#m2,.finding,.said" instruct="Does the message sentence (the fragment whose id starts with #m) make claims that are BACKED or UNSUPPORTED by the other fragments? Name the source ids and quote the shortest backing passage. Meeting turns name their speaker; every fragment is prefixed with its id." from="">
</slack:transform>

<slack:copy id="m3" class="message">These numbers exclude the load-test window on 2026-08-22 14:00–15:00 UTC.</slack:copy>

<slack:paste select="#m3" />

<slack:transform select="#m3,.finding,.said" instruct="Does the message sentence (the fragment whose id starts with #m) make claims that are BACKED or UNSUPPORTED by the other fragments? Name the source ids and quote the shortest backing passage. Meeting turns name their speaker; every fragment is prefixed with its id." from="">
</slack:transform>

<slack:copy id="m4" class="message">We don't need to revisit the pool size before Q4 unless traffic doubles.</slack:copy>

<slack:claim by="nate" standing="judgment" scope="checkout capacity">
<slack:paste select="#m4" />
</slack:claim>

